From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 22:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] video: logo: replace Tux with the R36S boot mark

RelicOS's boot splash, frame 1. The 224-colour Linux logo is the picture
fbcon paints the moment the panel lights (~3.3 s into the kernel on the
R36S, "Console: switching to colour frame buffer device"), which makes it
the earliest image this boot chain can show: mainline U-Boot has no video
stack for the RK3326 VOP, and userspace comes ~0.3 s later. So the product
logo goes where Tux was.

The PPM is the R36S mark alone (124x36, 121 colours, cropped from the
640x480 artwork by board/r36s/splash/make-splash.py); the black around it
is the console's own background, and fbcon=logo-pos:center,logo-count:1
on the command line puts it where the artwork had it. The kernel Image
grows by ~5 KiB instead of ~300 KiB for the full frame.

Not for upstream: this is branding, not a fix. Kept as a source-file
replacement rather than a new LOGO_* Kconfig entry because the arm64
defconfig already selects LOGO_LINUX_CLUT224 and nothing else in the tree
cares which picture that symbol carries.
---
--- a/drivers/video/logo/logo_linux_clut224.ppm
+++ b/drivers/video/logo/logo_linux_clut224.ppm
@@ -1,1604 +1,4468 @@
 P3
-# Standard 224-color Linux logo
-80 80
+# RelicOS boot logo, frame 1: cropped from r36s-mark-640x480.png box x258-381 y222-257; background was rgb(0, 0, 0)
+124 36
